(3199016, 444984, 48228, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice, and so bright, and so well focused.....<br/>I love this one, but adore the other two.....Especially the "blue".....</td>', 'Very, very nice, and so bright, and so well focused.....I love this one, but adore the other two.....Especially the "blue".....', '2007-01-09 05:45:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199060, 445382, 23458, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Pug-H:</b></div><hr/><i> Well, at least you weren''t too hungover to go up the hill and take this magnificent shot so early in the morning. Well done, Sam. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Heheh.... it''s hard to be TOO hungover when you haven''t gone to sleep yet :).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-09 06:51:11.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Pug-H: Well, at least you weren''t too hungover to go up the hill and take this magnificent shot so early in the morning. Well done, Sam.   Heheh.... it''s hard to be TOO hungover when you haven''t gone to sleep yet :).', '2007-01-09 06:49:57.000000', '2007-01-09 06:51:11.000000', 0),
(3199091, 444274, 57851, '<td valign="top">Never would I have thought this one was yours... But very well done=)</td>', 'Never would I have thought this one was yours... But very well done=)', '2007-01-09 07:18:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199093, 441690, 31829, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments guys and gals.  This is a little gem I found outside the Washington, DC area.  The thought of creatively lighting it at night sounds interesting, but I''d be afraid to go back here at night. ;-)  It wasn''t posted, but I''m sure it''s private property and in the DC area, anything suspicious really brings the cops out in force.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments guys and gals.  This is a little gem I found outside the Washington, DC area.  The thought of creatively lighting it at night sounds interesting, but I''d be afraid to go back here at night. ;-)  It wasn''t posted, but I''m sure it''s private property and in the DC area, anything suspicious really brings the cops out in force.', '2007-01-09 07:21:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199185, 441110, 6870, '<td valign="top">This is really nice! I love the atmosphere here so much. Congratulations!</td>', 'This is really nice! I love the atmosphere here so much. Congratulations!', '2007-01-09 08:24:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199188, 441110, 58098, '<td valign="top">man its reaaly nice :o, keep the good working...</td>', 'man its reaaly nice :o, keep the good working...', '2007-01-09 08:25:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199189, 444775, 6870, '<td valign="top">I''m glad to see a portrait amongst the ribbons. Well done and congratulations!</td>', 'I''m glad to see a portrait amongst the ribbons. Well done and congratulations!', '2007-01-09 08:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199234, 444074, 62642, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  The noisiness was on purpose.  And the funny thing is, I did consider composition quite a bit in this picture.  No biggie...I think everyone just has a different eye.  I, for example, am turned off by all of what I see as overprocessing in the other direction on this board, all the extreme colors and intensity.  I''m just more attracted to the strange, the experimental, the grainy, and even the understated.  As poorly as this did in the challenge, it is my number three shot so far...LOL...proof of how unpopular my work is on this board!  No problem...I''m going to keep on forcing it on everyone anyway!  BWAH-HAHAHAHA!</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  The noisiness was on purpose.  And the funny thing is, I did consider composition quite a bit in this picture.  No biggie...I think everyone just has a different eye.  I, for example, am turned off by all of what I see as overprocessing in the other direction on this board, all the extreme colors and intensity.  I''m just more attracted to the strange, the experimental, the grainy, and even the understated.  As poorly as this did in the challenge, it is my number three shot so far...LOL...proof of how unpopular my work is on this board!  No problem...I''m going to keep on forcing it on everyone anyway!  BWAH-HAHAHAHA!', '2007-01-09 08:49:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199375, 438248, 42495, '<td valign="top">To add to what Falc and Larus already said (and I agree), the egrit looks a bit unnatural, from the bluish cast to the feathers.  While overall the background is distracting, the biggest thing that pulls me from the subject is the blown out area at the base of the egrit''s neck and the grass to the left.  Our eyes are drawn to areas of high contrast in photographs; which works ok for most of the neck, but the very first thing I look at is the white in the background.</td>', 'To add to what Falc and Larus already said (and I agree), the egrit looks a bit unnatural, from the bluish cast to the feathers.  While overall the background is distracting, the biggest thing that pulls me from the subject is the blown out area at the base of the egrit''s neck and the grass to the left.  Our eyes are drawn to areas of high contrast in photographs; which works ok for most of the neck, but the very first thing I look at is the white in the background.', '2007-01-09 09:41:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3199798, 445383, 61234, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pawdrix:</b></div><hr/><i> What planet do you live on? I need to plan a vacation soon and that place looks cooler than anything we have here on Earth.<br/> <br/>Hope I didn''t hurt your feelings? Noticed that you didn''t mark your negative comments here as helpful. Hope you can see the positive in the negatives? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comments. This was taken along the southern Rhode Island shoreline. I go there often to study the receding light on the wet rocks. It does look surreal to me at times depending on the amount of colors at sunset. I was lucky with this one to tap the strong evening hues on the rocks.<br/> <br/>I welcome feedback, negative or otherwise. The one negative comment on this image wasn''t particularly helpful since I did very little post-processing on this image.  The original looks almost the same. I generally shy away from over-processing an image and prefer to take lots of pictures to insure the results I''m after. I was hoping to respond, but have to wait until after the challenge to do so.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for taking the time to comment.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-09 11:22:52.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by pawdrix: What planet do you live on? I need to plan a vacation soon and that place looks cooler than anything we have here on Earth. Hope I didn''t hurt your feelings? Noticed that you didn''t mark your negative comments here as helpful. Hope you can see the positive in the negatives?   Thanks for your comments. This was taken along the southern Rhode Island shoreline. I go there often to study the receding light on the wet rocks. It does look surreal to me at times depending on the amount of colors at sunset. I was lucky with this one to tap the strong evening hues on the rocks. I welcome feedback, negative or otherwise. The one negative comment on this image wasn''t particularly helpful since I did very little post-processing on this image.  The original looks almost the same. I generally shy away from over-processing an image and prefer to take lots of pictures to insure the results I''m after. I was hoping to respond, but have to wait until after the challenge to do so. Thanks again for taking the time to comment.', '2007-01-09 11:21:53.000000', '2007-01-09 11:22:52.000000', 0),
(3200009, 441819, 24454, '<td valign="top">Man, I really like this!   The color tones are so beautiful and I love how the lighting spotlights the crumpled up leaf!   Boy these dpc''ers are harsh critics, aren''t they!  I think this is tons better than 5.6!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Man, I really like this!   The color tones are so beautiful and I love how the lighting spotlights the crumpled up leaf!   Boy these dpc''ers are harsh critics, aren''t they!  I think this is tons better than 5.6! ', '2007-01-09 11:53:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3200019, 445384, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is very pretty.  Love the mood that the lighting creates - and it adds a nice glow to the wood too.  Have you ever had a chance to get closer and take a picture square on of the statue?  I bet that would be gorgeous!  The only thing that is a distraction is the stuff at the top of the pic.<br/> <br/>Can''t stop staring at the statue!</td>', 'This is very pretty.  Love the mood that the lighting creates - and it adds a nice glow to the wood too.  Have you ever had a chance to get closer and take a picture square on of the statue?  I bet that would be gorgeous!  The only thing that is a distraction is the stuff at the top of the pic. Can''t stop staring at the statue!', '2007-01-09 11:54:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3200068, 437355, 66857, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments! This was my first entry, had a little trouble with the sizing. I''ll get it eventually!</td>', 'Thanks for the comments! This was my first entry, had a little trouble with the sizing. I''ll get it eventually!', '2007-01-09 12:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3200312, 441110, 40490, '<td valign="top">That... is beautiful; I love every bit of it!</td>', 'That... is beautiful; I love every bit of it!', '2007-01-09 12:36:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3200551, 441819, 40683, '<td valign="top">Didn''t have time to comment during the voting, but I gave this a 7.  It definitely deserved a higher score, IMO.  The colors are wonderful!</td>', 'Didn''t have time to comment during the voting, but I gave this a 7.  It definitely deserved a higher score, IMO.  The colors are wonderful!', '2007-01-09 13:46:28.000000', NULL, 0),
