(3232562, 444964, 15029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>This scene is a real beauty. The sunset, the goose (I''m guessing, and the tree line. The exposure is spot on, the color is just right. There is only one issue that caused this photo to not reach its full potential, which has already been commented on. The focus, instead of being on the goose or the tree line is on the tree in the front of the frame. This draws the viewers focus to be drawn to the wrong place. It may have been better to make sure the focus was on the goose, and possibly moved a little to the right to get the tree out of the frame.<br/> <br/>Nice job and keep shooting,<br/> <br/>Mark<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the CC! This scene is a real beauty. The sunset, the goose (I''m guessing, and the tree line. The exposure is spot on, the color is just right. There is only one issue that caused this photo to not reach its full potential, which has already been commented on. The focus, instead of being on the goose or the tree line is on the tree in the front of the frame. This draws the viewers focus to be drawn to the wrong place. It may have been better to make sure the focus was on the goose, and possibly moved a little to the right to get the tree out of the frame. Nice job and keep shooting, Mark ', '2007-01-14 23:49:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3232609, 444070, 15029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC!<br/> <br/>This is an interesting subject, which his suffering from a lack of focus. There is nothing that draws the viewers eye. The colors are very nice, but the focus is just not there. When you are thinking about how to take a photo of a given subject, think about what you want the final shot to look like. Don''t just point your camera at an interesting subject and shoot. Be deliberate.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting,<br/> <br/>Mark</td>', 'Greetings from the CC! This is an interesting subject, which his suffering from a lack of focus. There is nothing that draws the viewers eye. The colors are very nice, but the focus is just not there. When you are thinking about how to take a photo of a given subject, think about what you want the final shot to look like. Don''t just point your camera at an interesting subject and shoot. Be deliberate. Keep shooting, Mark', '2007-01-15 00:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
